<div id="features" class="features">
  <section class="feature" aria-labelledby="capture-title">
    <div class="copy">
      <h2 id="capture-title">Mark up the web.</h2>
      <p>Twine is natively integrated with Safari. Highlight any text on any webpage and recall it later.</p>
      <ul class="checks" role="list">
        <li><span>Enable the extension to view and create highlights.</span></li>
        <li><span>Share direct links to highlighted text with other Safari users.</span></li>
        <li><span>Revisit a page and your highlights stick</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="media">
      {% shot "capture", "mac", "Twine on a Mac with a website sidebar, a highlight list and a selected passage in the details pane.", "The Twine library with its website sidebar, highlight list and selected passage details.", false, "Mac · Your library, organized by source", 1960, 1280 %}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="feature feature-library" aria-labelledby="library-title">
    <div class="copy">
      <h2 id="library-title">Build and maintain your own library.</h2>
      <p>Every highlight goes into one library on your Mac and iPhone. Search for the words you remember, browse by website and page, or filter to today, the past week, or the past month.</p>
      <ul class="checks" role="list">
        <li><span><strong>Search everything</strong> in your library</span></li>
        <li><span><strong>Jump back to the source</strong> in one click</span></li>
        <li><span><strong>Find highlights in Spotlight</strong> and use them in Shortcuts</span></li>
        <li><span><strong>Recent highlights in the menu bar</strong> on Mac</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="media">
      {% shot "library-duo", "duo", "Twine on iPhone Duo with Wikipedia highlights on the left and the selected training-cost passage, source and actions on the right.", "iPhone Duo open in landscape orientation, with the library and selected highlight details visible side by side.", false, "iPhone Duo · Wikipedia highlights and the selected passage", 2000, 1407 %}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="feature feature-ai" aria-labelledby="ai-title">
    <div class="copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">Twine Pro</p>
      <h2 id="ai-title">Give AI tools access - through a local, read-only connection.</h2>
      <p>Ground your writing, research, or studying in the information you found worth keeping. AI Access allows any MCP compatible harness to read, source, and answer based on the information you've vetted.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="media media-settings">
      {% shot "ai-access", "window", "Twine's AI settings on a Mac with AI Access enabled, a local server URL and controls to copy connection settings or regenerate the token; no token value is displayed.", "Twine Settings > AI > AI Access, with the local server enabled and connection controls visible. Keep access tokens concealed; no chat response needed.", false, "Mac · Read-only access for connected AI tools", 1040, 1436 %}
    </div>
    <div class="ai-details">
      <ul class="prompts" role="list" aria-label="Example requests">
        <li>“What have I highlighted about pricing strategy? Cite the sources.”</li>
        <li>“Find the passage I highlighted about sleep and memory, and link me to it.”</li>
        <li>“Draft an outline from my highlights on urban planning.”</li>
      </ul>
      <ul class="checks" role="list">
        <li><span><strong>Local.</strong> Twine runs the connection on your Mac. Your library isn't uploaded to a developer-run server.</span></li>
        <li><span><strong>Read-only.</strong> AI tools can search and read. They cannot add, edit, or delete through this connection.</span></li>
        <li><span><strong>Off by default.</strong> Nothing is shared through AI Access until you turn it on.</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

</div>

<section class="band" aria-labelledby="privacy-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 id="privacy-title">Your data is yours.</h2>
    <div>
      <p>Your browser history is your business. All data is stored in your private iCloud database and we have no access to it.</p>
      <ul class="checks" role="list">
        <li><span>Highlights live in your private iCloud database.</span></li>
        <li>No trackers, ads, or analytics.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="note">Highlighted websites receive display-name and icon requests. Optional Apple diagnostics, support messages and public GitHub feedback are covered in the privacy policy. A connected AI tool handles what it reads under its own policy.</p>
      <p class="more"><a class="text-link" href="/privacy">Read the privacy policy</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
  <h2 id="faq-title">Questions about Twine</h2>
  <div class="faq-list">
    <details>
      <summary>Do I need an account? Where does my data live?</summary>
      <p>No account. Your highlights live on your devices and in your private iCloud database. Twine doesn't send your library to the developer. The <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> explains website lookups, optional diagnostics, support messages and connected AI tools.</p>
    </details>
    {%- if site.pricing %}
    {% include "draft/pricing-faq.njk" %}
    {%- endif %}
    <details id="faq-ai-tools">
      <summary>Which AI tools can connect to Twine?</summary>
      <p>Use a compatible tool on your Mac that supports local MCP servers over HTTP with bearer-token authentication. Cloud-hosted chat services can't reach Twine, because it only listens on your Mac. Some tools need a connector or config file; see the <a href="/docs#connect-an-ai-tool">connection guide</a>.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Can an AI tool change my highlights?</summary>
      <p>No. AI Access is read-only. Tools can search, list, read, and export your highlights, but can't add, edit, or delete them through this connection. A tool with the token can read your whole library; turn AI Access off or replace the token to revoke access.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Do I need Apple Intelligence?</summary>
      <p>Only to write or refresh on-device AI context. You can read a note synced from another device without generating it again. Highlighting, the library, sync, and AI Access all work without it.</p>
    </details>
    <details id="faq-iphone-sync">
      <summary>When do highlights sync between my devices?</summary>
      <p>On Mac, highlights sync while Twine is running. On iPhone, highlights made in Safari sync the next time you open Twine. Select text and tap Twine in Safari's page menu, then open the app to upload. Use the same Apple Account on both devices; see the <a href="/docs#sync-with-icloud">sync guide</a>.</p>
    </details>
    <details id="faq-browsers">
      <summary>Does Twine work in other browsers?</summary>
      <p>Twine is built for Safari. Chrome, other Chromium browsers, and Firefox aren't supported in this release.</p>
    </details>
    <details id="faq-private-browsing">
      <summary>Does Twine work in Private Browsing?</summary>
      <p>No. Twine doesn't save or show highlights in Private Browsing.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Does it work on every web page?</summary>
      <p>It works on standard web pages with selectable text and permission to run in Safari. Twine leaves text fields alone. If a page's text or surrounding context changes, the highlight may not reappear on the page, but it stays in your library.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Are there limits?</summary>
      <p>A single highlight can be up to 5,000 characters, with up to 500 highlights per page. Twine saves up to 30 new highlights a minute; auto-highlight on Mac skips selections over 1,000 characters.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Which devices and languages does Twine support?</summary>
      <p>Mac with macOS {{ site.macOS }} and iPhone with iOS {{ site.iOS }}. Twine is available in English, German, Spanish, French, and Russian. See the <a href="#requirements">system requirements</a>.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>How do I get help?</summary>
      <p>Email <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>. Twine is made by one developer, and you'll hear back from him directly. There is no live chat or guaranteed response time. You can also read the <a href="/docs">docs</a>, <a href="{{ site.feedbackUrl }}">send public feedback on GitHub</a>, or visit <a href="/support">support</a>.</p>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>

